# Edera zone kernel variant: CPU-throughput (compute-bound, non-preemptible, low tick).
#
# Build-time deltas that help compute-bound work and can't all be reproduced at runtime:
# static PREEMPT_NONE (drop PREEMPT_DYNAMIC's per-call overhead, fewest preemption points),
# a 100Hz tick (fewer timer VM-exits in the guest than 1000Hz), and NUMA balancing off
# (removes background page-table scanning; also a sysctl, but compiled out here). NO_HZ_FULL
# is deliberately NOT set: it is inert without a housekeeping CPU and a nohz_full= cmdline,
# and its guest benefit is marginal -- add a separate multi-vCPU variant if that is tested.
# CONFIG_PREEMPT_DYNAMIC is not set
CONFIG_PREEMPT_NONE=y
CONFIG_HZ_100=y
# CONFIG_NUMA_BALANCING is not set
